    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d782">

                <pb facs="0849" n="750" sameAs="frus:frus1936v02/pg750"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">352.115/148: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Third Secretary
                        of Embassy in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wendelin</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-10-30T20:00:00-05:00">October 30, 1936—8
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>180. In a telegram received by Department October 28,<anchor n="78"
                        xml:id="d782-f1"/> the Consul General at Barcelona reports that the
                    International Banking Corporation has received a communication from the
                    Industrial Cotton <pb facs="0850" n="751" xml:id="pg751"/> Committee in
                    Barcelona stating that it had assumed possession, for the purpose of
                    distribution, of cotton taken over in Barcelona.</p>
                <p>Please bring the matter to the attention of the Foreign Office and say that in
                    the event that the American shippers do not receive payment from the authorities
                    in Barcelona this Government will be under the necessity of looking to the
                    Government of Spain for payment in full of all cotton taken over.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Carr</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
